FaxMail 2.3

		    Send faxes for free via email

FaxMail is a small Tk/Tcl program to help you send faxes for free via
email.  With FaxMail you can write a message, attach an image or two,
include a postscript document, then send the whole lot off as an email
to be delivered as a fax message (if your target fax number is
covered).  It works using the TPC remote printing service (www.tpc.int).

This message announces the release of version 2.3.  Changes in this 
version include: support for image inclusion (via ImageMagick), sanity
check for target fax number, renaming of executable from faxmail to 
FaxMail to avoid clash with hylafax package.

FaxMail is released under the GNU GPL.  Download the source from the
FaxMail homepage:

               http://wol.ra.phy.cam.ac.uk/FaxMail/

or from the TPC client software pages: 
   ftp://ftp.tpc.int/tpc/client/unix/FaxMail-2.3.tar.gz
   http://www.tpc.int/clients/index.html

Please report any bugs to mcdavey@mrao.cam.ac.uk

