GJH wrote:
> 
> for example a string : 'thisisastring'  where I want the first four
> characters : this.
> 

Sed works nicely:

	echo thisisastring | sed 's/\(....\).*/\1/'

The \(....\) part means save the first 4 characters (due to the for . )

The .* just matches the rest of the string

The \1 means write out what was matched by what was in the
first set of \(  \)


- Doug



