We'd like to send output directly from our DEC-Unix Alpha2100 to our LPS
17/600 via the printer's i.p. address.  In other words, I'd like to print
directly to the 17/600 without using DEC's LPS software.

Can someone send me a printcap (or some other lpr trick) that supports this
approach?

Direct network printing works fine with HP laser jets by using printcap
phrases :rp=text: and  :rm=netprinter: where netprinter is an /etc/hosts or
DNS name associated with the printer's i.p. address.  In the HP world,
"text" (and its companion "raw") have special meaning to the print engine
that allows correct interpretation of the incoming data stream, so this
works fine.  But the 17/600 does not recognize the word "text" or "raw" so
I'm thinking there might be some other way to do this.

Any help would be greatly appreciated.

Andy





