Sorry Andy, but you'll still need at least some of the PrintServer
software to provide boot images for the printers ! If you go to
http://www.printers.digital.com and look in the software/drivers
section, you'll find PrintServer Software for DEC Unix - this also adds
in the relevant items for printcap etc. Once you've actually booted the
printer (the DEC Unix software does this over BOOTP/TFTP) you can then
print to it using IP.

The software is available free of charge if you download it, and as far
as I recall, no licence PAK is required - the purchase of the
PrintServer licences you for the software.

Chris
